# Open this file in Neovim (>= 0.9) with kulala.nvim installed.
# LazyVim / lazy.nvim will load it automatically for *.http and *.rest.
#
# Keymaps inside this file (buffer-local, leader = <Space> by default):
#   <Space>Rs  send the request the cursor is on
#   <Space>Ra  send every request in this file, top to bottom
#   <Space>Ro  open the response scratchpad
#
# If a keymap does nothing, check :messages — usually it means the
# server is not running. Start it with:  make run
#
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Workflow for the PATCH and GET-by-id examples:
#
#   1) Press <Space>Ra once. The CREATE requests (#1, #2) write real
#      rows; #3 (LIST) prints them with their ids.
#   2) Open the response for #3, copy any "data1" UUID, paste it over
#      the PASTE-UUID-HERE placeholder in #4–#7.
#   3) Press <Space>Ra again (or <Space>Rs with the cursor on one
#      block) to re-run with the real id.
#
# No response-variable chaining, no plugin lock-in, works in any
# version of kulala.nvim.
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

@host = http://localhost:8080

### Health check
GET {{host}}/healthz

### 1) Create a product — the response is the source of the id for #2-#5
POST {{host}}/product
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Espresso Beans 1kg",
  "description": "Single-origin Ethiopian roast",
  "sale_price": 24.50,
  "price": 29.90
}

### 2) Create a minimal product (no optional fields) — for testing the "patch with nulls" case
POST {{host}}/product
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Plain Mug",
  "price": 9.99
}

### 3) List all products (sanity check the DB has data)
GET {{host}}/product

### 4) Get by id — replace PASTE-UUID-HERE with a real one (copy from #1 or #3)
GET {{host}}/product/PASTE-UUID-HERE

### 5) Patch by id — change only the price
PATCH {{host}}/product/PASTE-UUID-HERE
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "price": 31.50
}

### 6) Patch by id — null out description and sale_price (explicit clear)
PATCH {{host}}/product/PASTE-UUID-HERE
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": null,
  "sale_price": null
}

### 7) Patch by id — invalid (negative price), expect 422 INVALID_PRICE
PATCH {{host}}/product/PASTE-UUID-HERE
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "price": -1
}

### 8) Patch a non-existent id, expect 404 PRODUCT_NOT_FOUND
PATCH {{host}}/product/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "price": 1
}
